  "notes": [
    "Scope: 12 repo Pydantic models. Request: APIKeyCreate, APIKeyUpdate, RateLimitUpdate, UserCreate, UserUpdate, UserTierUpdate. Response: APIKeyRead, KeyUsageRead, RateLimitRead, TierRead, UserRead, UserProfileRead.",
    "No nested repo models: no field of these 12 models references another repo model (no list[Model], no Model-typed field). Enums in api_keys/enums.py are not used by any in-scope field.",
    "Field order follows Pydantic v2 (pydantic 2.13.4 in uv.lock): annotations collected over reversed(__mro__). For class X(TimestampSchema, Base) the MRO is X, TimestampSchema, Base, BaseModel, so the order is Base fields, then TimestampSchema fields (created_at, updated_at), then X's own fields. Applies to APIKeyRead and KeyUsageRead. Derived from Pydantic rules, not executed.",
    "Inherited fields carry the line of the parent declaration; 'declared_in' gives file::Class of that declaration.",
    "No Field(alias=...) and no alias_generator in any schema file: every alias is null.",
    "Annotated[X, Field(...)] fields: required=false only when Field(default=...) appears inside Annotated (TierBase/TierUpdate/UserUpdate style); Annotated with Field without default and no '=' is required.",
    "'X | None' without a default is required=true and nullable=true: UserRead.tier_id, APIKeyRead.last_used_at, APIKeyRead.last_used_ip.",
    "Routes returning dict[...] without response_model= have no repo response model (return annotation is dict, not a repo model): e.g. create_api_key, get_api_key, get_key_analytics, get_user_summary. APIKeyResponse, APIKeyWithPermissions, KeyUsageAnalytics, UserAPIKeySummary exist in api_keys/schemas.py but no route declares them, so they are out of scope.",
    "get_rate_limit declares response_model=RateLimitRead and return annotation 'dict[str, Any] | None'; response_model wins, so the response model is RateLimitRead.",
    "auth/login body is form data (OAuth2FormDep + remember_me Form()), not a repo Pydantic model.",
    "fastcrud.PaginatedListResponse is an external generic (not a repo model); its type argument is listed in route_models.",
    "Not in the given route list: interfaces/api/__init__.py:9-10 includes auth.oauth_router from crudauth (library router, conditional on OAuth config). Not covered here.",
    "Response JSON schema caveat: TimestampSchema.created_at/updated_at have @field_serializer returning 'str | None'; FastAPI's output (serialization) schema may show them as string (nullable) rather than date-time. Declared type is recorded as datetime."
  ]
